  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.4.15: Rebuilt against FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.15\n- ADDED: quantum Monte Carlo, option pricing and the risk engine run on the topological backend: amplitude estimation reads its logical-qubit probabilities\n\nv0.4.14: magic-state T injection applies T; rejected distillation batches stay rejected\n- CHANGED (breaking type): MagicStateDistillation.applyTGate returned the data qubit unrotated. The new applyTGateToQubit applies the exact T through TopologicalOperations.tGate, and applyTGate calls it; TGateResult.OutputState is now a TopologicalOperations.Superposition, since a single fusion tree cannot hold the T phase. GateFidelity still carries the magic state's fidelity\n- CHANGED: distill15to1 returned an improved state even when the syndrome check rejected the batch. DistillationResult gains Accepted, and a rejected batch keeps the input fidelity. distillIterative keeps only accepted batches, ignores partial batches and returns an Error when too few pass; supply several times 15^rounds states for a reliable run\n- Requires FSharp.Azure.Quantum v1.4.14+",
